{title: Once in Royal David's City}
{artist: Cecil Frances Alexander}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Once in royal [D]David's [G]city
[C]Stood a lowly [G]cattle [D]shed
[G]Where a mother [D]laid her [G]baby
[C]In a manger [G]for His [D]bed
[G]Mary [C]was that [G]mother [D]mild
[G]Jesus [C]Christ her [G]little [D]child[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]He came down to [D]earth from [G]heaven
[C]Who is God and [G]Lord of [D]all
[G]And His shelter [D]was a [G]stable
[C]And His cradle [G]was a [D]stall
[G]With the [C]poor and [G]mean and [D]lowly
[G]Lived on [C]earth our [G]Saviour [D]holy[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]And through all His [D]wondrous [G]childhood
[C]Day by day like [G]us He [D]grew
[G]He was little, [D]weak and [G]helpless
[C]Tears and smiles like [G]us He [D]knew
[G]And He [C]feeleth [G]for our [D]sadness
[G]And He [C]shareth [G]in our [D]gladness[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]And our eyes at [D]last shall [G]see Him
[C]Through His own re[G]deeming [D]love
[G]For that Child so [D]dear and [G]gentle
[C]Is our Lord in [G]heaven a[D]bove
[G]And He [C]leads His [G]children [D]on
[G]To the [C]place where [G]He is [D]gone[G]
{end_of_verse}
